# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-15), from board item 1.36; the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: Finder and Mail are docked side by side, and the person works framed on Mail, so Finder's window is out of view. They would rather
# Arbor left Finder alone and add a rule for that, which does not rearrange what is arranged. Then Arbor dies, so nothing is put back, and
# Finder starts again, so its window has another number: nothing but its place says that Arbor put it there. Arbor is started
# again. From now on it ignores Finder, so nothing would ever fetch that window: it has to come back into view first.
# Finder's windows have a toolbar. macOS stops them 52 points above the bottom of the display, where a plain window stops 28 or 32 above.
# Reference: issue #3 (no lost window), T61. Window ids start at 101.
open Finder 920x436
open Mail
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
zoom 102
expect hidden 101
rule add Finder ignore
expect ok
expect docked 101
expect hidden 101
flush
crash 101
expect ok
# 103 is Finder's window.
expect visible 103
expect visible 102
# And it is left alone from here on.
zoom 102
expect visible 103
dock 103 left
expect fail
# The same with a plain window, which stops lower.
open Notes
dock 104 right
zoom 102
expect hidden 104
rule add Notes ignore
flush
crash 104
expect visible 105
